{
	title: 'Preserve the reading position through viewport reflow',
	spec: "On viewport reflow (including phone rotation and keyboard resizing), the transcript preserves its pre-reflow reading position. If only the top edge is within 40 CSS pixels, keep that exact top distance; if only the bottom edge is within 40 CSS pixels, keep that exact bottom distance. The threshold is inclusive. If neither or both edges are close, preserve the text character/row at the visible viewport midpoint at the new midpoint, accounting for changed wrapping and font metrics rather than preserving a scroll fraction or absolute scrollTop. Native caret/Range geometry provides a text anchor; non-text/blank areas use the nearest retained element and its relative position, and removed anchors fall back to a clamped content-centre position. Impossible edge/centre targets clamp to the available scroll range. Anchor state is captured before reflow and refreshed for deliberate scrolling, content changes and tab changes; resize-induced scroll events must not overwrite the pre-reflow anchor. Browser scroll anchoring must not compete with explicit restoration, and any running glide is cancelled on resize. Native observers are cleaned up when the transcript unmounts; importing a module creates none. Browser tests verify exact/near top and bottom, the inclusive 40px threshold, middle text through width changes and both-near/short content cases, in both rotation directions. App width is capped by its layout container so a stale larger visual-viewport width cannot expand the layout viewport and trigger zoom when returning from landscape. Markdown high-water floors follow task fn's layout-local rule so obsolete height does not corrupt edge distances.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Real bidirectional rotation caught stale --app-width feedback: a width of 844px carried into portrait made the layout/visual viewport remain 844px and zoom out. max-width:100% on App prevents that. It also caught Markdown streaming min-height retaining the portrait peak after wrapping changed; task fn now scopes peaks to width/font layout.'
	],
	needs: ['4s', 'cw', 'fn']
